    "explanation": "The rider's claim is upheld and the $6.00 cancellation fee is refunded. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 300 seconds (EV-TRIP-00407, platform_policy.free_wait_sec 300, matching fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec of 300 for the TRANSPORT_HUB zone class). POL-NS-01 limb (c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the 'arrived' marker. On EV-GPS-00407 the driver held inside the 150 m arrival radius in a single unbroken run of 290 seconds, from 17:02:20 to 17:07:10, against a cancellation at 17:07:18 — a shortfall of 10 seconds, which is EV-GPS-00407's own derived shortfall_sec. The driver's answer — that the trip record's rounded wait_time_min of 5.0 minutes should count the clock to the cancellation — does not save the fee: on his own timestamps (arrived 17:02:20, cancelled 17:07:18) the dwell is 298 seconds, still two seconds short of the 300-second minimum. The fee is therefore not chargeable under POL-NS-06 and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present; the same conclusion follows from POL-NS-01 limb (c). Arrival itself was never disputed: 30 consecutive in-radius fixes satisfy POL-NS-02, and the arrival marker is not false (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0, no fix at the marker more than 300 m from the pin or moving at 15 km/h or above), so no POL-NS-05 false-arrival referral arises. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 displaces it; the anti-farming check is not reached (and would not trip — 1 no-show termination against 120 completed trips in 30 days, a rate of 0.008). The driver's request to escalate under POL-NS-09(b) is declined: there is no direct contradiction between admissible artifacts on dwell, because POL-NS-01(c) fixes the clock to the GPS fixes and the trip record's rounded 5.0 minutes is fully consistent with 298 seconds, and on either reading the 300-second minimum was not served, so no open question remains for a reviewer. On impairment: EV-ADVIS-00407-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and carries no fact here — the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation it would permit is unavailable and was not needed, there being only one in-geofence interval — while the artifacts that carry the deciding fact, EV-GPS-00407 and EV-TRIP-00407, both stand at weight 1.0 with no issue codes, so nothing in POL-NS-08 caps confidence and no escalation under POL-NS-09(a) or (e) is engaged. The rider's own track (34 fixes, all 895–905 m from the pin, zero qualifying fixes inside the 200 m rider-presence radius) would fail POL-NS-04 limb (c), but that clause is not reached: the rider posted no locating or coordinating message, so limb (a) fails on the face of the chat log (EV-CHAT-00407), and in any event POL-NS-06 refunds regardless of rider presence, which disposes of the driver's 'Rider was nowhere' point. Amount: EV-FARE-00407 shows cancellation_fee $6.00, total_charged $6.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd $0.00; the $6.00 line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of $6.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect, and no POL-GEN-05 issue is raised by the $6.00 line being refunded. The refund is the cancellation-fee line only — $6.00. The monetary effect ($6.00) is below the execution_threshold_sgd of $8.00, so it executes automatically on issue. No referral is produced: the arrival marker was not false (POL-NS-05) and the cancellation reason EXCESSIVE_WAIT is one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises, so no driver-education item arises."
