    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the $6.00 Jurong East cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full. The driver receives no compensation, and the case is not escalated.\n\nThe facts. The trip was accepted at 17:00:40 and the driver reached the interchange private-hire bay at 17:02:20; he cancelled at 17:07:18 with the reason code EXCESSIVE_WAIT. Arrival is not in dispute, and the driver's own trace (EV-GPS-00407, weight 1.0, 100% coverage at a 10 s cadence, no gaps) supports it: 30 consecutive fixes inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius. Limbs (a) and (b) of POL-NS-01 therefore hold.\n\nThe waiting period. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 300 seconds - trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec is 300, which is also the TRANSPORT_HUB minimum in the fee schedule, and not the 180 s default. POL-NS-01(c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least that period, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. The trace shows a single unbroken in-geofence run of 290 seconds, from 17:02:20 to 17:07:10: a shortfall of 10 seconds. The driver's answer - that the trace simply ends 8 seconds before cancellation so the true hold is longer - does not save the fee: on the trip record's own events (arrived 17:02:20, cancelled 17:07:18) the driver was on station 298 seconds, still two seconds short of 300. Nor is trip_record.wait_time_min = 5.0 a measurement; POL-NS-01(c) fixes the clock to the GPS fixes, and a rounded summary field cannot extend it.\n\nThe outcome. POL-NS-01 limb (c) fails, so the fee is not chargeable under the anchor clause, and POL-NS-06 refunds it in full: the effective dwell (290 s) is shorter than the free waiting period (300 s), and that is so whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider replied. The rider's silence in chat, and his device's fixes sitting 895-905 m from the pin, do not change this. POL-NS-04 does not apply, because no rider message was sent (limb (a) fails), but the rider does not need it, and the rider's track being outside the presence radius decides only the exoneration route, not the fee.\n\nThe money. The ledger EV-FARE-00407 shows cancellation_fee $6.00, total_charged $6.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd $0.00. The full $6.00 is refunded. That line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of $6.00, so there is no fare-integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d) - the figure is right, the charge is not. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays 80% of the $6.00 (i.e. $4.80) only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not; the anti-farming check does not trip in any event (1 no-show termination in 30 days against 120 completed trips). The monetary effect, $6.00, is below the $8.00 execution threshold of POL-GEN-05, so the refund executes automatically.\n\nNo escalation and no referral. The driver asks for human review under POL-NS-09(b), saying the record's 5.0 minutes and the trace's 290 seconds contradict each other on dwell. They do not: POL-NS-01(c) expressly resolves how the dwell is measured, and both readings fall short, so there is no unresolved conflict. The other triggers are absent - confidence is above the 0.70 floor, there is no same-pair dispute pattern, no anti-farming pattern, and the deciding artifacts EV-GPS-00407 and EV-TRIP-00407 are unimpaired at weight 1.0. No referral fires either: POL-NS-05's false-arrival triggers are not met (the marker's timestamp matches the first in-geofence fix, and the driver was inside the radius and stationary), and POL-NS-07 does not trip. The missing advisory EV-ADVIS-00407-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) makes POL-NS-06(i)'s accumulation test unavailable, but nothing turns on it - the trace shows a single interval (run_count 1). Two rider-side claims were discarded by the referee for citing that weight-0.0 artifact without naming its issue code; they concerned the driver's 'enforcement officers' statement and